  "caveats": [
    "A simulation of deposited pathway models does not show that stimulus amplitude leaves memory intact in cells.",
    "The pre-registered rule refutes the claim: N = 23 completed models, same = 0.2608695652173913, lost = 0.6086956521739131, gained = 6. Refutation requires N >= 12 and lost >= 0.40. That holds. The pass rule also required same >= 0.50 and lost <= 0.20.",
    "gained = 6 means six models had a higher memory count at scale 10 or 50 than at scale 100. That is the direction of the claim's remark that some models formed more memories under weaker stimulation. The registered rule still refutes, because the lost fraction is above 0.40.",
    "The count is UCS-based memories plus associative memories only. Pairing, transfer and consolidation memories are not included. The paper's pooled percentages can use a wider set of memory phenotypes. This exclusion was stated before the run.",
    "One completed model, BIOMD0000000483, has a memory count of zero at all three scales and is included in the same fraction. The registration did not drop zero counts.",
    "Four of 27 size-eligible models failed to integrate, below the pre-registered half-failure cutoff. Assignment-rule species and a collapsed solver step are the failures. libroadrunner getRatesOfChange does not fire SBML events. Each epoch is one adaptive integration with the clamped species held fixed."
